    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Jacksonville-FL/Learning-Designer_JR103538": {
      "title": "Learning Designer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nDepartment Office of Teaching & Learning (OTL) Compensation $62,000.00 to Negotiable Annual   General Description / Primary Purpose   The Learning Designer in the Office of Teaching and Learning provides instructional consultation and develops and facilitates faculty professional development across disciplines and instructional modalities. The position works with faculty, departments, and faculty groups to identify teaching and learning challenges and apply evidence-based strategies that strengthen teaching practice, student engagement, learning, and persistence. This is an on-campus position.   Job Function   Design, coordinate, and facilitate workshops, institutes, book clubs, faculty learning communities, and other professional learning opportunities related to effective teaching and student success.    Provide confidential, individualized consultation to faculty on instructional strategies, course organization, assessment, student engagement, and other teaching and learning concerns.    Work with individual faculty members, departments, and faculty groups to identify instructional challenges, recommend practical, evidence-based strategies, and assess the effectiveness of instructional changes.    Conduct voluntary, confidential, and formative classroom observations and mid-semester feedback activities to support instructional improvement.    Review instructional materials and advise faculty on course organization and the effective use of Canvas and other instructional technologies to support clarity, engagement, accessibility, and student learning.    Develop practical guides, training materials, consultation tools, and other faculty resources.   Contribute to professional learning for new faculty, adjunct faculty, graduate teaching assistants, and other instructional personnel.    Collaborate with OTL colleagues, academic units, and campus partners to identify teaching needs and coordinate appropriate programming and support.    Assess faculty-development programs and services and maintain current knowledge of research and emerging practices relevant to higher education.    Other duties as assigned. During declared campus emergencies, this position may be required to perform specific job-related duties at a designated off-campus location or place of residence.   Core Competencies   Experience teaching and applying evidence-based teaching practices, adult learning principles, learning sciences, and instructional strategies in higher education or another adult-learning setting. Experience designing and facilitating engaging professional development in in-person and virtual settings. Ability to analyze teaching and learning challenges and provide practical, context-sensitive guidance. Ability to establish trust and communicate effectively with faculty, staff, and campus partners. Excellent consultation, facilitation, presentation, interpersonal, written communication, and organizational skills. Ability to manage multiple consultations, programs, and projects while meeting deadlines. Familiarity with learning management systems, preferably Canvas, and other instructional technologies used in higher education. Knowledge of accessibility and inclusive teaching practices.   Supervision Received   General supervision. The incumbent independently manages a variety of complex responsibilities within established guidelines, exercises professional judgment while work is in process, and receives direction on new assignments and institutional priorities.     Required Qualifications Master's or Bachelor's degree and 2+ years of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219.  Preferred Qualifications and Experience A  master's degree in education , instructional design, curriculum and instruction, educational technology, higher education, faculty development, or a related field; college or university teaching experience; experience providing instructional consultation or professional development to higher education faculty; and experience conducting formative classroom observations or providing structured feedback on teaching. Required Application Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Professional References   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
