    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Jacksonville-FL/Title-IX-and-Civil-Rights-Case-Manager_JR103514": {
      "title": "Title IX and Civil Rights Case Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nDepartment Equal Opportunity & Access Compensation $50,000.00 to Negotiable Annual   Case Management and Support Services Serves as the primary case manager for individuals involved in matters addressed by the Office of Title IX and Civil Rights. Conducts intake meetings with complainants, respondents, witnesses, and other affected parties. Explains University policies, procedures, rights, options, available resources, and resolution processes. Coordinates supportive measures and related accommodations as appropriate. Maintains regular communication with involved parties throughout the resolution process. Monitors implementation of supportive measures, no-contact directives, and other interim actions. Makes referrals to campus and community resources. Documents interactions and maintains accurate records within the case management system.   Case Coordination and Compliance Support Coordinates meetings, hearings, alternative resolution processes, and other case-related activities. Monitors deadlines and ensures timely progression of cases in collaboration with leadership. Prepares correspondence, notices, and case-related documentation. Maintains confidential records and assists with compliance-related recordkeeping requirements. Assists with data collection, reporting, audits, assessments, and compliance reviews. Participates in implementation of institutional responses to reports involving discrimination, harassment, retaliation, sexual misconduct, stalking, dating violence, and domestic violence. Collaborates and maintains effective relationships with campus partners to support compliance efforts and coordinated responses.   Education, Outreach, and Prevention Participates in development and delivery of educational programs related to discrimination, harassment, retaliation, sexual misconduct, interpersonal violence, and civil rights compliance. Participates in training initiatives for students, faculty, staff, and campus partners. Assists with development of educational materials, resource guides, website content, and outreach materials. Supports prevention and awareness initiatives designed to increase understanding of reporting options, available resources, and institutional policies.   Investigative Coordination Assists investigators with complaint investigations responsibilities as assigned. Conducts interviews, gathers information, reviews documentation, and prepares investigative materials.  Provides administrative coordination for evidence organization, investigative records, and hearing and resolution processes.   Policy-Making and Interpretation Provides information regarding University policies, procedures, and complaint resolution processes. Assists in interpreting and applying established policies and procedures and refers complex policy questions to appropriate Office personnel.   Program Direction and Development Assists with implementation, assessment, and continuous improvement of case management practices, educational initiatives, outreach activities, and compliance-support functions. Provides feedback regarding operational processes and opportunities to improve service delivery and efficiency.   Marginal Functions Serves on University committees, task forces, and workgroups as assigned. Attends professional development programs, conferences, and training opportunities. Assists with emergency response activities and other duties as assigned in support of the Office and University mission.   Supervision Exercised May provide guidance, training, and work coordination to student employees, interns, graduate assistants, or temporary personnel as assigned. Does not exercise direct supervisory authority over full-time employees.     Required Qualifications Master's or Bachelor's degree and 2+ years of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219.    Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator   This position has been designated as a Campus Security Authority (CSA). This position has been designated as a CSA because it involves significant responsibility for student and campus activities and/or responsibility for campus security. As such, any person in this position must report to the University Police Department a crime or an incident that might be a crime that he/she becomes aware of. This position has a reporting requirement because the University believes that responsibility for students, campus activities and/or campus security will make the holder of this position someone members of the University community will see as an authority figure and someone to whom they can seek help. A CSA is not expected to investigate or determine whether a criminal incident actually took place. A CSA ’ s responsibility is a duty to report. All positions designated as CSAs are required to complete an online or in - person training session. For more information concerning training or CSA designations, please contact the Clery Act Compliance Manager at (904) 620-1423 or clery@unf.edu.   Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Jacksonville-FL/BCH-Graduate-Program-Coordinator_JR103518": {
      "title": "BCH Graduate Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nDepartment Brooks College of Health, Operations Compensation $48,000.00 to Negotiable Annual   General Description / Primary Purpose The Graduate Program Coordinator supports graduate student recruitment, enrollment, retention, progression, and graduation efforts across the Brooks College of Health through comprehensive advising coordination, academic progress monitoring, communication management, and student success initiatives.   Job Functions :   Student Advising and Academic Support Serve as a primary point of contact for graduate students regarding academic policies, registration processes, degree requirements, and university resources. Assist students with registration-related processes, including applying and removing advising or program holds, issuing registration overrides, resolving registration issues, and supporting academic success initiatives. Provide timely and accurate information regarding college, university, and graduate program requirements. Identify, troubleshoot, and resolve routine advising and administrative issues while escalating complex concerns to the appropriate program director or university office. Serve as a student advocate by connecting students with academic and support resources that promote retention, persistence, and degree completion. Support graduate student onboarding and orientation activities in collaboration with graduate program directors and university partners. Assist with initiatives designed to improve enrollment yield, retention, persistence, and student engagement.   Academic Progress Monitoring Maintain and monitor student degree progress records using Degree Works and other university systems. Collect, analyze, and use student data as appropriate to support advising and administrative functions, ensuring compliance with FERPA regulations. Prepare reports and documentation related to enrollment, advising, progression, retention, graduation, and other student success metrics. Verify completion of degree requirements and coordinate with program directors and university offices as needed. Assist students with graduation application processes and related requirements. Maintain accurate student academic records in accordance with university policies and procedures.   Collaboration and Program Support Collaborate with graduate program directors, faculty, the Graduate School, BCH Academic Advisors, Enrollment Services, and other university partners to support graduate student success. Participate in graduate program-related meetings, advising meetings, student success initiatives, and professional development activities. Assist with the development, assessment, and continuous improvement of graduate student services and program processes. Perform other related duties as assigned to support departmental operations and Brooks College of Health graduate programs.   Required Qualifications Master's or Bachelor's degree and 2+ years of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219.    Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
