    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Jacksonville-FL/Event-Services-Coordinator_JR103510-1": {
      "title": "Event Services Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nDepartment University Center, Events-OPS Compensation $18.00 to Negotiable Hourly   General Description The Event Services Coordinator serves as the Herbert University Center's primary on-site representative during evening and weekend events. Working independently, this position supports successful event execution by providing exceptional customer service, coordinating event support services, ensuring the facility remains safe, secure, and event-ready, and serving as the lead operational contact during assigned shifts. As the primary point of contact for clients, guests, vendors, and University support departments, the Event Services Coordinator exercises sound judgment, coordinates resources, resolves routine operational issues, and facilitates communication among stakeholders to ensure a positive event experience. The Coordinator is entrusted with managing event and facility operations during assigned shifts, making informed decisions within established guidelines and escalating issues when appropriate. This position works primarily evenings and weekends based on event schedules and operational needs. Job Functions Event Operations & Client Service Review event schedules, event orders, room diagrams, and service requests to ensure event readiness and accuracy. Serve as the primary on-site contact for clients, guests, vendors, and event participants during assigned events. Provide responsive, professional customer service by addressing requests, resolving concerns, and coordinating resources to support successful event execution. Monitor event activities and proactively identify, troubleshoot, and resolve routine event, facility, and customer service issues, escalating concerns when appropriate. Assist with event setup modifications and operational adjustments to accommodate client needs and changing event requirements. Provide basic audiovisual setup, operation, troubleshooting, and equipment support for standard meeting and presentation technologies. Communicate event updates, client concerns, facility issues, and operational needs to appropriate HUC staff. Perform occasional physical duties, including lifting, moving, pushing, and pulling furniture or equipment in support of event operations. Facility Operations & Safety Open, close, secure, and monitor the facility in accordance with established procedures. Conduct routine facility rounds to monitor event activity, remain accessible to clients and guests, and identify operational concerns. Coordinate with custodial, maintenance, University Police, catering, and other support departments to address facility and event-related needs. Monitor building conditions and address concerns related to room access, equipment needs, furniture arrangements, guest assistance, and event logistics. Follow established University and HUC safety procedures and respond appropriately to emergencies, incidents, and building-related concerns. Document incidents, safety concerns, service disruptions, and operational issues occurring during assigned shifts. Operational Oversight & Administration Serve as the responsible HUC representative during assigned shifts, demonstrating professionalism, initiative, sound judgment, and accountability. Exercise independent judgment in managing event, facility, and customer service matters during assigned shifts, making informed decisions within established guidelines and escalating issues when necessary. Coordinate the activities of student employees and event support staff to support successful event execution and facility operations. Monitor contracted event services and verify that event requirements are delivered as planned. Complete shift reports, event logs, incident documentation, and other required records. Assist visitors with information regarding HUC services, event locations, facility amenities, and University resources. Maintain familiarity with facility policies, event procedures, operational standards, and customer service expectations. Communicate operational, staffing, safety, and event-related information to supervisors and event planning staff for appropriate follow-up. Perform other related duties in support of event and facility operations. Core Competencies Customer Service Excellence Event Operations & Logistics Independent Decision-Making Problem Solving & Resourcefulness Communication & Interpersonal Skills Professional Judgment Initiative & Accountability Time Management & Organization Attention to Detail Adaptability & Flexibility   Required Qualifications   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Jacksonville-FL/Event-Services-Associate_JR102881": {
      "title": "Event Services Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nDepartment University Center Compensation $18.27 to Negotiable Hourly   General Description The Event Services Associate supports the planning and execution of conferences, meetings, and special events within the Herbert University Center (HUC) by ensuring accurate event setup, operational readiness, and exceptional client service. This role serves as an on-site operational support position, providing day-to-day oversight of student event staff and assisting with facility readiness under the guidance of event planning staff to support University and external clients. The position primarily works Tuesday through Saturday with an emphasis on evening hours, with schedules adjusted as needed to meet event and operational demands. Job Functions Event Operations & Execution Coordinate and execute daily event setups and breakdowns for conferences, meetings, and special events, ensuring all rooms, furnishings, and equipment are accurately arranged according to event specifications. Review event orders and setup requirements prior to each event to ensure accuracy, completeness, and operational feasibility. Perform physical duties including lifting, moving, pushing, and pulling furniture and equipment weighing 50+ pounds, and remaining on foot for extended periods during event operations. Serve as the on-site event point of contact during assigned shifts, resolving operational issues and ensuring seamless event execution when event planning staff are not present. Ensure all requested client services are delivered accurately, on time, and in accordance with established HUC standards. Function occasionally as the on-site audiovisual technician during some events by operating and supporting sound, projection, and presentation systems in accordance with event requirements. Staff Supervision & Leadership Hire, train, schedule, and provide day-to-day supervision for approximately eight OPS/student event setup staff members. Assign tasks, provide clear instructions, and monitor performance during event setups and operations to ensure efficiency, safety, and accountability. Support the development of student staff by modeling professionalism, providing coaching, and enforcing policies and procedures consistently. Facilities, Equipment & Inventory Management Ensure proper maintenance, cleanliness, organization, and storage of event furnishings, equipment, storage areas, and event spaces. Conduct periodic inventories of furniture, supplies, and audiovisual equipment; document and report damaged, missing, or malfunctioning items and replacement needs. Set up, operate, break down, and properly store audiovisual equipment, verifying functionality and readiness for client use. Building Operations, Safety & Emergency Response Assist with building operations including opening, closing, monitoring, and clearing the facility in accordance with HUC procedures. Conduct regular facility rounds during events to remain visible, accessible, and responsive to client and guest needs. Follow and implement established emergency and safety procedures and serve as a Building Emergency Coordinator when required. Customer Service & Administrative Support Provide courteous, professional customer service to clients, guests, staff, and vendors in person, by phone, and via email. Assist visitors with general information regarding HUC services and the University of North Florida, including event rentals, tours, and directional assistance. Document event-related issues, client concerns, or requested changes and communicate them promptly to the event planning team. Provide front desk coverage and answer phones. Manage time effectively and complete assignments in compliance with all HUC and UNF policies and procedures. Perform other related duties as assigned to support event and facility operations. Supervisory Responsibilities Supervision Exercised: Provides direct supervision to approximately eight OPS/student event setup staff members, including task assignment, performance monitoring, and on-the-job training. Supervision Received: Works independently in the performance of routine duties; refers complex, unusual, or non-routine issues to a supervisor for guidance or resolution. Core Competencies Customer Service Event Operations Support Communication Skills Team Leadership and Collaboration Time Management and Organization Attention to Detail   Required Qualifications High school diploma and 2+ years of relevant experience. Or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219. This position primarily works evening shifts Tuesday through Friday and includes Saturday as part of the regular schedule, with hours varying based on events. Please confirm that you are able and willing to work this schedule   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Jacksonville-FL/Coordinator-of-Athletics-Development-Events-and-Donor-Engagement_JR103503": {
      "title": "Coordinator of Athletics Development Events and Donor Engagement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nDepartment Athletics, Development Compensation $42,000.00 Annual   Essential Duties and Responsibilities Fundraising & Special Events Management Coordinate, manage, and execute all Athletics Development fundraising events that support donor cultivation, stewardship, engagement, and revenue generation. Serve as the primary event coordinator for Athletics special events, including but not limited to:  Osprey Booster events Hall of Fame activities Golf tournaments and outings Donor receptions and appreciation events Coaches' caravans and community engagement events Athletic facility dedications and ribbon cuttings Student-athlete recognition events Alumni and letterwinner events Hospitality functions associated with athletic competitions Special donor experiences and VIP events Athletics fundraising campaign celebrations Giving Day and 904 Day events Athletics community outreach and promotional events UNF Arena Suite event coordination Develop event timelines, project plans, budgets, and operational procedures. Coordinate vendors, catering, facilities, audiovisual needs, transportation, permits, and event logistics in an effort to maximize event revenue. Collaborate with Athletics External Operations, Strategic Communications, Ticketing, Facilities, Compliance, and University Advancement to ensure successful event execution. Manage event registrations, guest lists, sponsorship benefits, seating plans, and post-event reporting. Evaluate event effectiveness through participation, engagement, and fundraising outcomes. Hospitality Operations Oversee donor and VIP hospitality for all home athletic events and special functions. Coordinate game-day hospitality spaces, premium seating areas, donor lounges, and special guest experiences. Ensure exceptional customer service for donors, alumni, sponsors, university leadership, and community partners. Manage hospitality inventories, event materials, signage, gifts, and recognition items. Coordinate food and beverage service for donor and prospect events. Stewardship & Donor Engagement Coordinate donor stewardship programs designed to cultivate, recognize, and retain Athletics donors. Plan and execute donor appreciation events and recognition opportunities. Assist with donor communications, acknowledgments, impact reports, and stewardship initiatives. Support personalized donor experiences and engagement opportunities throughout the year. Giving Day & 904 Day Support Assist in planning and executing UNF Giving Day, 904 Day, and other Athletics-focused annual giving campaigns. Coordinate promotional events and participation initiatives supporting annual fundraising goals. Support volunteer and ambassador engagement efforts. Track participation metrics and campaign results. Intern & OPS Staff Management Recruit, train, supervise, and evaluate interns and OPS staff supporting Athletics Development initiatives. Develop work schedules and assign responsibilities for events and operational support. Provide mentorship and professional development opportunities. Ensure staff deliver exceptional customer service and represent UNF Athletics professionally. Development Operations Support Provide day-to-day support for Athletics Development operations. Assist with donor database management, event registration platforms, and donor communications. Coordinate department meetings, calendars, travel arrangements, and administrative projects. Support fundraising officers with event preparation, stewardship efforts, and donor engagement activities. Assist with strategic initiatives and special projects as assigned.     Required Qualifications Master's or Bachelor's degree and 2+ years of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219.  For more information about this position, please contact Derek Marinatos at derek.marinatos@unf.edu.   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator   This position has been designated as a Campus Security Authority (CSA). This position has been designated as a CSA because it involves significant responsibility for student and campus activities and/or responsibility for campus security. As such, any person in this position must report to the University Police Department a crime or an incident that might be a crime that he/she becomes aware of. This position has a reporting requirement because the University believes that responsibility for students, campus activities and/or campus security will make the holder of this position someone members of the University community will see as an authority figure and someone to whom they can seek help. A CSA is not expected to investigate or determine whether a criminal incident actually took place. A CSA ’ s responsibility is a duty to report. All positions designated as CSAs are required to complete an online or in - person training session. For more information concerning training or CSA designations, please contact the Clery Act Compliance Manager at (904) 620-1423 or clery@unf.edu.   The holder of this position is responsible for any NCAA and Atlantic Sun Conference bylaws and guidelines that a member of the UNF Athletic Compliance Department provides in addition to all UNF regulations. The individual must also assure that NCAA, Conference and UNF regulations are followed to the best of their knowledge and any violations thereof are reported to UNF Athletic Compliance. Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
