    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Jacksonville-FL/Custodial-Worker_JR103488": {
      "title": "Custodial Worker",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nDepartment Housing & Residence Life Compensation $16.00 Hourly   General Description / Primary Purpose Work performing housekeeping duties including cleaning restrooms, lounges, student apartments, common-use areas, carpet and tile floors.   Job Functions Clean & Maintain Restrooms Clean/sanitize/disinfect fixtures, walls, floors, mirrors, & shelves Clean/fill soap, paper towel dispensers Empty wastebaskets Report problems due to malfunction/damage/wear Report on lighting failures   Clean & Maintain Floor Lounges Vacuum floors Empty wastebaskets Clean walls, floors & doors Report about problems due to damage/wear Report lighting failures Arrange furniture Shampoo upholstered furniture Wipe tables & chairs   Clean & Maintain Public Lounge Appliances Clean & check microwaves Clean & check stoves Empty wastebaskets Report problems due to malfunctions/damage/ wear Report on non-functioning lights Clean sinks, counter tops, cabinets & vent hoods   Clean & Maintain Halls, Common Areas, Postal Facility, Stairwells, Courtyards, Parking Areas, Elevators, Building Entrance Areas & Ground Areas Vacuum floors & upholstered furniture Dust tables, windows sills, arms/legs of chairs, fire extinguisher & water hose cabinets Damp clean vinyl-covered furniture Shampoo upholstered chairs Sweep stairway & steps Sweep/mop tile floors Clean drinking fountains Clean stairway handrails Clean walls & doors Clean elevator doors, cabins & door tracks Remove debris & sweep entrance walks & steps Keep entrance mats clean Empty trash containers & sand urns Report non-functioning light bulbs Pressure washes external concrete areas Dispose of contaminated trash & waste materials   Clean & Maintain Rooms, Apartments & Suites Remove debris, sweep and vacuum Spot clean walls, floors & doors Clean, defrost & deodorize refrigerator Clean & check stoves for proper operation Clean sinks, countertops, cabinets & vent hoods Clean, sanitize, & disinfect fixtures, walls, floors, mirrors & shelves Vacuum & clean air conditioner closets Shampoo carpets   Clean Glass Windows, Doors, & Window Blinds Use proper cleaners to remove grime/smudges/other substances from glass Clean surfaces Use proper equipment & take safety precautions when cleaning hard to reach surfaces Clean glass Clean window blinds   Perform Additional Floor Cleaning & Maintenance Duties Spray buffs resilient tile floors Strip & rewax resilient tile floors Shampoo carpets Use pile brush vacuum to lift carpet pile Clean grout on tile   Performs Cleaning According to Blood Borne Pathogen Regulations Clean up spills of human bodily fluids Use proper personal protective equipment during cleanup Handle & dispose of removed fluids & cleaning materials as biowaste Attends refresher training on blood borne pathogens Inoculated against Hepatitis B   Marginal Functions Special set-up requests Provide manpower during Housing events Clean up after events Work orders Check-outs and check-ins Help keep residential break and storage areas neat and clean This position is designated as a Tier 2 respondent for designated campus emergencies & events. In the event of a declared campus emergency, the position incumbent will make every effort to return to campus when directed.   Required Qualifications Completion of ninth (9th) grade or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219. Some positions may require possession of a classified driver’s license appropriate to a type of vehicle operated.   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
