    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Gainesville-FL/Computer-Programmer_JR103027": {
      "title": "Computer Programmer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-26\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nDepartment Institute of Utility Security and Resilience (IUSR) Compensation $85,000.00 to $95,000 Annual   General Description/ Primary Purpose: The position supports the data transfer, analysis, presentation, and governance for the overall Full-Scale Pavement testing effort. This role coordinates with research staff to develop rational database structures and programs based on data base software, general programming languages, and data presentation software. This position is located on-site in the Pavement Research Unit of the FDOT State Materials Office in Gainesville, FL. Job Functions: The position requires a highly motivated and organized employee who is responsible for the following tasks: Development and maintenance of database systems in addition to analytical tools and technologies. Creating interactive data visualization and reporting tools. Development of documentation and data governance practices/procedures (such as software documentation, data workflows, etc.). Integration of artificial intelligence techniques into data analysis techniques. Support for automated reporting and data analysis processes. Implementation and ongoing development of new technologies and infrastructure to improve pavement data collection, processing, analysis, and reporting, with a focus on continuous improvements in this area moving forward.   Required Qualifications This position requires effective communication skills (both verbal and in writing). The Computer Programmer position will need to develop effective working relationships throughout the Full-Scale Pavement Testing Program and across the State Materials Office. Minimum qualifications require a bachelor’s degree in a relevant field with applicable work experience. A graduate degree and research experience are preferable.    Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator Pursuant to Florida Statute 1010.35, this position requires additional information from all applicants seeking research or research-related positions prior to an interview or offer of employment. Applicants MUST fully complete the Foreign Influence Review section of their application. Additional documents (e.g., passport) may be required based on form responses.     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Jacksonville-FL/Senior-Engineer-Technical-Designer_JR103044": {
      "title": "Senior Engineer Technical Designer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nDepartment Physical Facilities, Engineering Compensation $22.98 to Negotiable Hourly   General Description / Primary Purpose This position performs senior-level technical engineering support related to the maintenance, organization, and stewardship of campus engineering and construction records. The role serves as the custodian of the University’s digital drawing and infrastructure documentation, including campus utility maps, digital flat files, and Operations and Maintenance (O&M) manuals. Job Functions ·         Engineering Records and Mapping Management Serves as the custodian of the University’s repository of digital engineering and construction records, including campus utility maps, digital flat files, and Operations and Maintenance (O&M) manuals. Maintains the campus map by continuously updating utility and infrastructure information as the campus evolves. Ensures engineering records are accurate, current, properly organized, and stored in designated systems and file locations. Reviews and culls digital files to confirm correct placement, version control, and long-term usability. ·         Technical Engineering Support Utilizes the AutoCAD environment to review, interpret, and manage engineering and infrastructure documentation. Maintains awareness of CAD licensing requirements and monitors license usage as needed. Provides engineering documentation and technical support to Facilities staff, designers, contractors, and other stakeholders upon request. Responds to requests for records and documentation promptly, often on short notice. ·         Underground Utility Coordination Serves as the University’s liaison to Underground Utility (UGU) organizations. Coordinates with university employees, designers, and contractors to assist in the identification and location of underground utilities. Visits construction sites as needed to photograph underground utilities prior to site grading to support accurate documentation and mapping. ·         Work Orders and Project Support Supports engineering work orders and construction-related activities by supplying accurate records, maps, and supporting documentation. Provides supplementary technical assistance to the department and campus partners as needed. Responds to campus maintenance emergencies by providing engineering records, maps, and utility information as required. During declared campus emergencies, this position may be required to perform specific job-related duties at a designated off campus location or place of residence.         Required Qualifications High school diploma and 4+ years of relevant experience. Or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219.   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Gainesville-FL/Senior-Instrumentation-Hardware-Engineer_JR103028": {
      "title": "Senior Instrumentation Hardware Engineer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nDepartment Institute of Utility Security and Resilience (IUSR) Compensation $75,000.00 to $83,000 Annual   General Description/ Primary Purpose: This position will focus on development of DAQ hardware (sensors, I/O devices, chassis, etc.) as part of the overall APT effort, including the HVS machines, HVS Test Tracks, and both Test Roads. The role will be responsible for the design, selection, testing, installation, calibration, and maintenance of the DAQ hardware. They will work closely with the Senior Instrumentation Software Engineer to ensure seamless integration of the comprehensive DAQ effort. In the field troubleshooting of the DAQ hardware is required. This position is located on-site in the Pavement Research Unit of the FDOT State Materials Office in Gainesville, FL. Job Functions: The position requires a highly motivated and organized employee who is responsible for the following tasks: Maintenance of existing APT DAQ hardware such as sensors, controls boards Coordinate the testing and calibration of sensors Develop Installation Protocols focused on embedded sensors Development of Lessons Learned document detailing successes and failures of chosen sensors, calibration procedures, installation procedures, etc.   Required Qualifications This position will focus on development of DAQ hardware (sensors, I/O devices, chassis, etc.) as part of the overall APT effort, including the HVS machines, HVS Test Tracks, and both Test Roads. The Senior Instrumentation Hardware Engineer will be responsible for the design, selection, testing, installation, calibration, and maintenance of the DAQ hardware. They will work closely with the Senior Instrumentation Software Engineer to ensure seamless integration of the comprehensive DAQ effort. In the field troubleshooting of the DAQ hardware is required.   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator Pursuant to Florida Statute 1010.35, this position requires additional information from all applicants seeking research or research-related positions prior to an interview or offer of employment. Applicants MUST fully complete the Foreign Influence Review section of their application. Additional documents (e.g., passport) may be required based on form responses.     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
