    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Jacksonville-FL/Catering-Bartender_JR101781": {
      "title": "Catering Bartender",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-06-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nDepartment MOCA-OPS Compensation $25.00 Hourly     The Catering Bartender is part of the events and catering team at the Museum of Contemporary Art Jacksonville. This position ensures smooth and professional food and  beverage service during events and catering with an emphasis on high standards in appearance, hospitality, and customer satisfaction. Pay is hourly and is scalable based on size and scope of event. Pay and tips are paid out on a regular bi-weekly payroll schedule. Bartender Specific Duties: Mix drinks using an extensive range of ingredients including liquor, bitters, soda, water, sugar, and fruits, including standard and unique drinks. Keep bar area clean, safe, and organized Providing great customer service while maintaining control of the bar, serving drinks, and managing the financials. Mix all drinks based on the standard serving sizes, keeping drink costs at a minimum. Collect payment for drinks served and providing change as needed; Balance cash receipts; Maintain an accurate drawer throughout the event. Ability to think quickly, exercise good judgement and monitor patrons for overconsumption is essential. Previous experience with cash handling, ability to cash-out the cash drawer, making sure it balances with the POS system and note any discrepancies.  Check identification to verify legal age requirements for all customers  Keep a well-stocked bar with an adequate supply of liquor, beer, wine, mixers, ice, napkins, straws, glassware, and other accessories.  Slice, pit, and prepare fruit garnishes for drinks Complete alcohol inventories and communicate any resupply requests to the Venue Coordinator. General Responsibilities:  Maintain honesty and integrity, kindness, and a positive attitude, always create a good rapport with staff and guests.  Always ensure excellent customer service. Operate POS system, operate cash register, and provide accounting of sales if required. Accept payments, issue receipts, and return appropriate change when needed. Receive and resolve complaints concerning food, beverage, and service reporting all concerns to immediate supervisor and appropriate staff.  Always follow operational policies, procedures, and practices. Adhere to food and beverage practices in keeping with health and safety requirements, maintain recipes, portions, temperatures, and presentation maintaining consistency in guest experience. Immediately report all safety, deficiency, and maintenance concerns. Responsible for maintaining back of house inventory including stocking, moving supplies, ensuring all areas are well-kept, and reporting low inventory as needed. Assist in event and catering loading and unloading, setup and execution anticipating number of guests and customer needs as well as assist with take down and clean up at end of event/service.  Attend and all pre-shift meetings to ensure events flow smoothly.  Assist in ensuring that each event starts service on time as per the event plan. Inspect equipment for damage, checking equipment against inventory list before and after event. Maintain regular and punctual attendance.  Attention to detail. Perform all other duties as assigned by immediate lead, supervisor, and administration staff. Qualifications:  Cannot be a current UNF student for this position type .  Must be 21 or over.  A minimum of 1-year previous relevant experience in hospitality.  Must have good interpersonal skills, including good oral and written communication, ability to communicate well with people on all levels, and able to receive and fulfill orders.  High school diploma or equivalent preferred. Must be able to work a flexible schedule including days, evenings, and weekends as needed. Must have reliable transportation and able to work on-site and off-site events. Must be able to perform physical activities related to food and beverage service which includes, walking, standing, sitting, reaching, and kneeling for long periods of time, and lifting a minimum of 25 lbs. ServSafe Food Handler Certified required as well as Background Check.   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, gender identity/expression, sexual orientation, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Jacksonville-FL/Adjunct-in-Marketing_JR101318-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct in Marketing",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-06-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nDepartment Marketing & Logistics, Chair-OPS Compensation Negotiable     General Description/Primary Purpose: The Department of Marketing & Logistics is seeking to hire adjunct faculty. Appointment: Adjunct faculty are hired on a semester-by-semester basis, as needed, and are non-tenure-earning. Anticipated Start Date: The position is expected to begin on August 4th, 2025.  Position responsibilities include but not limited to: Teach assigned course(s) in accordance with the approved syllabus and course schedule Hold scheduled office hours with frequency and modality as negotiated with the acting program director and department chair. Working Hours:  Part-time Work Schedule:  Varies Supervision Exercised: This is not a supervisory role. Compensation : Adjunct faculty are paid a minimum of $1000 per credit hour. About the Department: For more information about the Department of Marketing, visit: https://www.unf.edu/coggin/marketing/index.html Required Qualifications: Graduate degree in the teaching discipline or in a closely related field. Preferred Qualifications: Professional-related managerial and teaching experience. Required Licensure: N/A Additional Application Materials Required: Applicants should be prepared to provide the following required documents: Current curriculum vitae Cover letter 3 Reference letters Official transcripts Names, phone numbers, and email address of three professional references will be requested during the application review stage. The selected candidate will be required to submit official transcripts (and, as applicable, U.S. degree equivalency evaluations) documenting the conferral of their qualifying academic credentials by the date of hire. Job Posting Close Date: Open until filled. Note: Adjunct postings may close at any time without notice. How to Apply: Applicants must submit an online application that includes all required documents and reference information. If you have any questions about this position, please contact Jasmine Justilien at 904-620-1334 or Jasmine.Justilien@unf.edu.    Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, gender identity/expression, sexual orientation, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
